The first, \emph{closure error} measures interferometric consistency over valid triplets $(i,j,k)$ and is defined as:
\begin{equation}
\varepsilon_{ijk}(p)=\mathcal{W}\!\left(\phi_{ij}(p)+\phi_{jk}(p)-\phi_{ik}(p)\right).
\end{equation}
where $\phi_{ij}$ is the wrapped phase of pair $(i,j)$, $\mathcal{W}(\cdot)$ wraps phase to $[-\pi,\pi)$. The reported closure error is the mean absolute wrapped closure residual, averaged over all valid pixels and all valid triplets.  Second, the \emph{unwrap success rate} quantifies the fraction of valid interferometric pixels that are successfully unwrapped,
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{USR}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{P}|}\sum_{(i,j)\in\mathcal{P}}\frac{|\Omega^{\mathrm{unwrap}}_{ij}|}{|\Omega^{\mathrm{valid}}_{ij}|},
\end{equation}
where $\Omega^{\mathrm{valid}}_{ij}$ is the valid-pixel mask before unwrapping and $\Omega^{\mathrm{unwrap}}_{ij}$ is the subset assigned reliable unwrapped phase by SNAPHU. Third, DEM quality is assessed using the \emph{normalized median absolute deviation} (NMAD) between the predicted elevation $\hat{h}$ and reference DEM height $h^{\mathrm{ref}}$,
\begin{equation}
e_h(p)=\hat{h}(p)-h^{\mathrm{ref}}(p),
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{NMAD}=1.4826 \cdot \mathrm{median}_{p\in\Omega_h}
\left(
\left|e_h(p)-\mathrm{median}(e_h)\right|
\right).
\end{equation}
where $\Omega_h$ denotes the valid comparison domain. Finally, the \emph{temporal residual} measures stack-level consistency with respect to an SBAS model,
\begin{equation}
r_{\Phi}=\mathcal{W}\!\left(\hat{\boldsymbol{\phi}}-\mathbf{A}\mathbf{x}^{*}\right),
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{TR}=
\frac{1}{|\Omega_{\Phi}|}
\left\|
r_{\Phi}
\right\|_{1},
\end{equation}
where $\mathbf{x}^{*}$ denotes the stack-level temporal solution obtained from the SBAS model, $\mathbf{A}$ is the SBAS design matrix, and $\mathcal{W}(\cdot)$ wraps residual phase to $[-\pi,\pi)$.












